<P><FONT 
                                face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" 
                                size=2><B>City of Villans and Other E3 Spotlights</B></FONT><BR><FONT 
                                face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" 
                                size=1>By Tucker Smedes<br>5/18/2004</FONT></P>


<a href="#1">City of Heroes</a><br>

<a href="#2">Random Game Coverage and Pics</a>
<br><br>

<a name="1"></a>
<strong>Interview with Chris Sutton</strong>
<br><br>

The City of Heroes expansion, City of Villains, is set to be released somewhere around a year from now.  At that time, Heroes will be able to battle Villains in awesome PvP battles.  I had the opportunity to talk with Chris Sutton, the Lead Artist for City of Heroes and City of Villains.  He was able to describe their current vision for what the game would end up looking and feeling like, which sounded very promising.
<br><br>

The way Chris explained the idea of the expansion to me was that Heroes start out and begin a story, and at the beginning they have some sort of special powers, which they can further develop as they grow.  Villains however will be a total flip of this, and will start out as people who aren't quite on the right side of the law, and may develop their powers in a different way.  
<br><br>

When going into more detail regarding PvP, he was able to provide some hints as to how it would play out, but not a lot of detailed specifics.  He told me there would be both areas Heroes couldn't go as well as areas Villains would not be permitted.  I wanted to find out if existing servers would have PvP added to them or if it would only occur on new servers, and to this he was able to say that they expected the expansion to fit right in with current content and current servers, however they may also add some new servers specifically for PvP.
<br><br>

One idea that stood out a bit when Chris was describing the PvP play to me was the fact that there would be aerial combat.  Characters with the flying ability would be able to attack from in the air; however there will be others who can use anti-air skills to bring them down.
<br><br>

The developers of CoV have talked about it being possibly released as a standalone game so people would be able to start out as a Villain, however as of right now that's not the design idea.  
<br><br>

I also wanted to know if a hero would ever be able to turn evil, and vice versa.  I was told that the idea was one they had definitely talked about; it wasn't too likely to happen.  The idea fits well and the concept would work, however it would be too hard to balance and would end up with multiple complications.
<br><br>

One feature they would be adding that definitely sparked my interest was the addition of "unique items of power."  What these will be, are items that will affect an entire Supergroup by adding something that benefits the entire group.  If there are 10 Villain Supergroups, there might only be 5 items… so the way it would work out, the Villains would be fighting amongst themselves to gain them to make their group stronger, however at the same time, the Heroes would be trying to obtain those items to weaken the Villains.
<br><br>

One question I had heard people wanting to know was if there would ever be the ability to re-spec, or change what points you put things into.  The answer to this was a tentative, "maybe."  The reason for his answer was that while they would like to allow it for people who accidentally chose something or people who tried something and found out they didn't like it… the flip side is they don't want to allow it solely for the reason that when creating your hero, you are starting a story and you can't exactly develop a power then suddenly change to one you liked better.  It makes sense if you look at it from the comic book point of view… what if Superman decided he didn't want x-ray vision but instead wanted the ability to walk through walls; that makes a bit too much of a change.
<br><br>

In addition to the entirely new Villains content, there will be some new hero content added when the expansion is released.  Among the additions will be a tailor.  In short, this will allow you to change the look of your costume.  Chris added that the every-few-month updates that are currently going on would definitely not change when the expansion is added.  He also included that there would likely be arenas added to current content, allowing for Heroes to vie in PvP before the release of CoV.
<br><br>

When asked about beta, they weren't able to provide much info, but did say that current CoH players would be the first ones invited to the CoV beta when it did launch.  It was also noted that, "there may be an open beta close to launch for a few weeks to a month or so, similar to how the CoH open beta was."

